 # CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT
 
+## 2026-05-19 Phase 1B-fix handoff cache removal
+
+This pass is a Phase 1B consistency fix only. It does not advance the `samplereverse` reverse-engineering mainline, does not enter Phase 1C/1E/1F or Phase 2, and does not implement artifact freshness or `lint-decision`.
+
+### Audit Result
+
+| check | result |
+|---|---|
+| `build_project_state()` handoff call | It previously called `build_handoff_status(state_dir)` after identity metadata and wrote the result into `task_packet["handoff_status"]`. |
+| cache timing risk | That snapshot is produced during `build`, before the usual final report and pytest-result writes, so it can become stale before archive. |
+| live status behavior | `status_summary()` still dynamically calls `build_handoff_status(state_dir)` and reads the live Markdown files at status time. |
+| downstream compatibility | `task_packet.json` keeps stable fields: `active_decision_packet`, `task_source`, `execution_scope`, and `expected_gpt_output`. |
+| freshness alternative | No sha256 freshness snapshot was added; the smaller fix is to avoid persisting the volatile handoff status in `task_packet.json`. |
+
+### Changes Made
+
+- Removed the `task_packet["handoff_status"] = build_handoff_status(state_dir)` write from `build_project_state()`.
+- Kept dynamic handoff parsing in `status_summary()` and CLI `status`.
+- Updated tests so generated `task_packet.json` must not contain cached `handoff_status`.
+- Added coverage that changing `codex_execution_report.md` after `build_project_state()` is visible through `status_summary()` without rebuilding.
+
+### Verification This Round
